# Phase 172 — pre-push build gate.
#
# WHY: pushing to main bypasses the required "lint & build" status check,
# because branch protection has enforce_admins=false. GitHub reports it as
#   remote: Bypassed rule violations for refs/heads/main:
#   remote:  - Required status check "lint & build" is expected.
# Vercel then deploys that commit immediately, while CI takes ~40s to report —
# so a broken bundle can reach production before anything flags it. This hook
# closes that window locally.
#
# Runs lint + a real vite build. The build is the part that matters: it is the
# only gate that resolves ESM import specifiers, which is exactly what the
# W5 file splits keep getting wrong (a module moved one directory deeper
# silently repoints every relative import — Phase 161, Phase 171).
#
# `npx vite build` rather than `npm run build` on purpose: the latter fires the
# postbuild chain (gen-version / prerender / indexnow), which has side effects
# we don't want on every push.
#
# Bypass when you genuinely need to: `git push --no-verify`.

npm run lint && npx vite build
